cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus build, these tests or the prediction registry, please cite it as below."
title: "Open Indus: reproducible tests on the Indus script"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible tests on the Indus script. It covers a corpus build of Mahadevan 1977 and the
  Wells/Fuls ICIT, held-out tests on a leak-free family split, a red-team reimplementation, a
  project-wide multiple-testing ledger, an atlas of closed routes and a hash-sealed registry of
  predictions for future finds. The script is not deciphered: no sign has a tested sound or
  meaning, and the language is not identified. The accompanying measurement paper (preprint,
  doi:10.5281/zenodo.24371567) reports how far the two editions disagree, how much random
  train/test splits leak through near-copies, and which questions the corpus is too small to answer.
type: software
